  "It took Puerto Rico and controlled Cuba after 1898, backed Panama's split from Colombia so it could build a canal, and under the Roosevelt Corollary sent troops into Caribbean and Central American countries many times. "
  "In the Cold War, Washington backed coups against governments it saw as communist or hostile, such as Guatemala's in 1954 and Chile's in 1973, and tried to overthrow Castro's Cuba. "
  "Many Latin Americans see this history as imperialism; US leaders presented it as defending the hemisphere's security.",
