  "In the Cold War, fear of revolution brought military dictatorships to Brazil, Chile, Argentina and other countries. They killed or 'disappeared' tens of thousands of people. "
  "Democracy returned in the 1980s, but debt crises and deep inequality fuelled swings between market reformers and left-wing leaders, from Chávez to Lula, and more recently to outsiders like Argentina's Javier Milei.",
